{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_59","type":"agent_message","text":"# Implementation Notes\n\n## Decisions Made\n- Added enqueue-time source-profile validation in `Engine::apply_action` for `WaterChangePercent`, while keeping `systems::water_change::validate_water_changes` as a defensive step-time guard for preloaded invalid queues.\n- Removed the DIC-driven alkalinity feedback from hourly chemistry so alkalinity now changes only through nitrification and water-change mixing.\n- Reworked daily filter fouling so `cleanliness_index` decays from detritus and shrimp bioload pressure, `clogging_index` accumulates during normal operation, and `CleanFilter` restores cleanliness proportionally to the requested intensity.\n- Extended water changes to mix `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total` using retained tank DO plus source-water saturation DO derived from the existing temperature-based saturation table.\n- Added targeted regressions for immediate bad-profile rejection, DO mixing on water changes, filter-cleanliness decay, queued fallback validation, and alkalinity stability under pure DIC drift.\n\n## Spec Deviations\n- None.\n\n## Testing\n- Verified with `PATH=/nix/store/jxrk3rflz1pv7xvbxhgkg6i2x95yhspz-rust-default-1.93.1/bin:/nix/store/pbqah1qk4b5y14fqinr1h8zvhqy71v81-gcc-wrapper-14.3.0/bin:$PATH cargo test`.\n\n---"}}
